-- ============================================================
-- Alonecraft 4.61 -- Rogue / Subtlety, part 2 of 6
--   Shadowstep   -> reduced chance to be hit instead of threat
--   Camouflage   -> also shortens Shadowstep and Shadow Dance
--   Elusiveness  -> also shortens Evasion and Shadow Dance
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md:
--   "Shadowstep: Threat no longer affected. Instead reduces your chance
--    to be hit."
--   "Camouflage: Also reduces the cooldown of Shadowstep and Shadow Dance."
--   "Elusiveness: Also reduces the cooldown on Evasion and Shadow Dance."
--
--
-- SHADOWSTEP (36554 -> the buff it triggers, 44373)
--
--   Shadowstep is three spells: 36554 is the cast (two TRIGGER_SPELL
--   effects plus the movement-speed aura, so all three of its effect slots
--   are occupied), 36563 is the +20% next-ability damage buff, and 44373
--   is the -50% threat buff.  The threat is entirely in 44373, so that is
--   the spell that gets rebuilt -- 36554 itself only needs its tooltip
--   rewritten.
--
--   44373 was a one-charge SPELLMOD_THREAT (aura 108, EffectMiscValue 2)
--   consumed by the next ability.  It becomes a plain timed defensive:
--   MOD_ATTACKER_MELEE_HIT_CHANCE (184) and
--   MOD_ATTACKER_RANGED_HIT_CHANCE (185) at -10% for 15 s.
--
--   A charge-consumed buff makes no sense for a passive avoidance aura, so
--   ProcCharges/ProcFlags/ProcChance are all cleared -- left at 1/16/100
--   the aura would vanish the first time the rogue landed an ability.
--
--   Effect 1's class mask (638714630 / 270) selected which abilities could
--   spend the threat charge.  Attacker-hit auras are not spell modifiers
--   and must not carry a mask, so all three of effect 1's words are zeroed,
--   as is EffectMiscValue1.
--
--
-- CAMOUFLAGE (13975, 14062, 14063) and ELUSIVENESS (13981, 14066)
--
--   Both keep every existing effect and gain their new cooldown reduction
--   in the free effect-3 slot as ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER (107) with
--   EffectMiscValue 11 (SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN).  Values are milliseconds and
--   carry the usual -1 offset (-2001 = -2 s).
--
--   No new family flags were needed: every target already owns a unique
--   rogue bit -- Shadowstep word B 512, Shadow Dance word B 33554432,
--   Evasion word A 32.  (Word A bit 5 is also on "Evasion TEST" and the
--   "Juju Escape" trinket; neither matters.)
--
--   CLASS-MASK COLUMN TRAP: EffectSpellClassMask{X}{n} is effect X, word n.
--   Effect 3's three words are therefore C1/C2/C3, and all three are
--   written explicitly below.
--
--   Evasion's cooldown lives in CategoryRecoveryTime (category 66) rather
--   than RecoveryTime; SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN is applied to both, so this works,
--   but it is the one line here worth confirming in game.
--
-- ============================================================


